Program to port: CBACT04C. Module name: port.generated.cbact04c

Context API (hand-written shell; this is the only I/O you have):
CBACT04C files.

category_balances   list[dict]  TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD (CVTRA01Y) in ascending key order
                    (TRANCAT-ACCT-ID, TRANCAT-TYPE-CD, TRANCAT-CD), i.e. the order a
                    sequential read of the indexed file returns
accounts            dict[int, dict]  ACCOUNT-RECORD (CVACT01Y) by ACCT-ID; update in place
xref_by_card        dict[str, dict]  CARD-XREF-RECORD (CVACT03Y) by XREF-CARD-NUM
xref_by_account     dict[int, dict]  CARD-XREF-RECORD by XREF-ACCT-ID (alternate key)
disclosure_groups   dict[(str, str, int), dict]  DIS-GROUP-RECORD (CVTRA02Y) by
                    (DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID as 10 chars, DIS-TRAN-TYPE-CD, DIS-TRAN-CAT-CD)
write_transaction(tran_record)  append a TRAN-RECORD (CVTRA05Y) to the sequential
                    transaction output file, in call order
parm_date           str, the job PARM (10 chars, e.g. '2022071800')
now()               current date-time (frozen for tests)
return_code         int, initially 0

port.runtime:
Hand-written runtime helpers available to the generated port (no business logic).

COBOL numeric semantics the port may need:
  fit(value, digits, scale, signed)  store a value into a PIC 9(n)V9(m) field: truncate
                                     toward zero to `scale` decimals and drop high-order
                                     digits beyond `digits` total digits (no ROUNDED).
  fit_rounded(...)                   same, but rounds half away from zero (COBOL ROUNDED).
  Abend                              raise to end the run abnormally (like CEE3ABD).
  rule(id)                           decorator linking a function to the rule it implements.

Record layouts (copybooks):
CVTRA01Y TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD (50 bytes)
  TRANCAT-ACCT-ID              9(11)          offset   0 size 11
  TRANCAT-TYPE-CD              X(2)           offset  11 size 2
  TRANCAT-CD                   9(4)           offset  13 size 4
  TRAN-CAT-BAL                 S9(9)V9(2)     offset  17 size 11
  FILLER                       X(22)          offset  28 size 22
CVACT03Y CARD-XREF-RECORD (50 bytes)
  XREF-CARD-NUM                X(16)          offset   0 size 16
  XREF-CUST-ID                 9(9)           offset  16 size 9
  XREF-ACCT-ID                 9(11)          offset  25 size 11
  FILLER                       X(14)          offset  36 size 14
CVTRA02Y DIS-GROUP-RECORD (50 bytes)
  DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID            X(10)          offset   0 size 10
  DIS-TRAN-TYPE-CD             X(2)           offset  10 size 2
  DIS-TRAN-CAT-CD              9(4)           offset  12 size 4
  DIS-INT-RATE                 S9(4)V9(2)     offset  16 size 6
  FILLER                       X(28)          offset  22 size 28
CVACT01Y ACCOUNT-RECORD (300 bytes)
  ACCT-ID                      9(11)          offset   0 size 11
  ACCT-ACTIVE-STATUS           X(1)           offset  11 size 1
  ACCT-CURR-BAL                S9(10)V9(2)    offset  12 size 12
  ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT            S9(10)V9(2)    offset  24 size 12
  ACCT-CASH-CREDIT-LIMIT       S9(10)V9(2)    offset  36 size 12
  ACCT-OPEN-DATE               X(10)          offset  48 size 10
  ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE          X(10)          offset  58 size 10
  ACCT-REISSUE-DATE            X(10)          offset  68 size 10
  ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT         S9(10)V9(2)    offset  78 size 12
  ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT          S9(10)V9(2)    offset  90 size 12
  ACCT-ADDR-ZIP                X(10)          offset 102 size 10
  ACCT-GROUP-ID                X(10)          offset 112 size 10
  FILLER                       X(178)         offset 122 size 178
CVTRA05Y TRAN-RECORD (350 bytes)
  TRAN-ID                      X(16)          offset   0 size 16
  TRAN-TYPE-CD                 X(2)           offset  16 size 2
  TRAN-CAT-CD                  9(4)           offset  18 size 4
  TRAN-SOURCE                  X(10)          offset  22 size 10
  TRAN-DESC                    X(100)         offset  32 size 100
  TRAN-AMT                     S9(9)V9(2)     offset 132 size 11
  TRAN-MERCHANT-ID             9(9)           offset 143 size 9
  TRAN-MERCHANT-NAME           X(50)          offset 152 size 50
  TRAN-MERCHANT-CITY           X(50)          offset 202 size 50
  TRAN-MERCHANT-ZIP            X(10)          offset 252 size 10
  TRAN-CARD-NUM                X(16)          offset 262 size 16
  TRAN-ORIG-TS                 X(26)          offset 278 size 26
  TRAN-PROC-TS                 X(26)          offset 304 size 26
  FILLER                       X(20)          offset 330 size 20

Verified business rules (the only specification):
[
 {
  "id": "BR-CBACT04C-001",
  "title": "Category balances are processed in account groups (control break on account ID)",
  "summary": "Category balance records are read one by one in key order. When the account ID changes, the account loaded before is written back with its interest (except on the very first record), the interest total is reset to zero, and the new account and its card cross-reference are read. Every record, including the first of a group, then goes on to rate lookup, and interest is only calculated when the rate is not zero.",
  "given": [
   {
    "text": "Category balance records are read one at a time, in key order, from the category balance file, which is indexed and read sequentially. The record key starts with the account ID, so all categories for one account come in together.",
    "fields": [
     "TCATBAL-FILE",
     "FD-TRAN-CAT-KEY",
     "FD-TRANCAT-ACCT-ID",
     "TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD"
    ],
    "literals": []
   },
   {
    "text": "At program start the last-seen account number is spaces and the first-time flag is 'Y'.",
    "fields": [
     "WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM",
     "WS-FIRST-TIME"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "Y"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "when": [
   {
    "text": "A category balance record is read and its account ID differs from the last-seen account number.",
    "fields": [
     "END-OF-FILE",
     "TRANCAT-ACCT-ID",
     "WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "N"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "then": [
   {
    "text": "If this is not the first account group, 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT runs for the account loaded before: it adds the accumulated interest total to the account's current balance, sets the current-cycle credit and debit to 0, and rewrites the account record. On the first group the first-time flag is only set to 'N'.",
    "fields": [
     "WS-FIRST-TIME",
     "WS-TOTAL-INT",
     "ACCT-CURR-BAL",
     "ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT",
     "ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT",
     "FD-ACCTFILE-REC",
     "ACCOUNT-RECORD"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "Y",
     "N"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The interest total is reset to 0 and the last-seen account number is set to the new account ID.",
    "fields": [
     "WS-TOTAL-INT",
     "WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM",
     "TRANCAT-ACCT-ID"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "0"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The account record for the new account ID is read by key from the account file into ACCOUNT-RECORD.",
    "fields": [
     "TRANCAT-ACCT-ID",
     "FD-ACCT-ID",
     "ACCOUNT-RECORD"
    ],
    "literals": []
   },
   {
    "text": "The card cross-reference for the account is read through the account-ID alternate key. Its card number is the one later copied into the card number of each interest transaction.",
    "fields": [
     "TRANCAT-ACCT-ID",
     "FD-XREF-ACCT-ID",
     "CARD-XREF-RECORD",
     "XREF-CARD-NUM",
     "TRAN-CARD-NUM"
    ],
    "literals": []
   },
   {
    "text": "For every category balance record, whether or not the account changed, the rate lookup key is built from the account's group ID and the record's category code and type code, and the interest rate is looked up.",
    "fields": [
     "ACCT-GROUP-ID",
     "FD-DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID",
     "TRANCAT-CD",
     "FD-DIS-TRAN-CAT-CD",
     "TRANCAT-TYPE-CD",
     "FD-DIS-TRAN-TYPE-CD"
    ],
    "literals": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Interest is calculated (and the fee step run) only when the interest rate found is not zero. Records with a zero rate add nothing to the account's interest total.",
    "fields": [
     "DIS-INT-RATE"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "0"
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "BR-CBACT04C-002",
  "title": "Account balance update with accumulated interest at account break",
  "summary": "When an account group ends because the next record belongs to a different account, the account's interest total is added to its current balance, the current-cycle credit and debit are set to zero, and the account record is rewritten. Because of how the loop is written, the last account group in the file is never updated.",
  "given": [
   {
    "text": "Each calculated monthly interest amount is added to an interest total for the account. The total holds 9 integer digits and 2 decimals, signed.",
    "fields": [
     "WS-MONTHLY-INT",
     "WS-TOTAL-INT"
    ],
    "literals": []
   }
  ],
  "when": [
   {
    "text": "1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT runs when a record for a new account arrives and it is not the first account group.",
    "fields": [
     "TRANCAT-ACCT-ID",
     "WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM",
     "WS-FIRST-TIME"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "Y"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "then": [
   {
    "text": "The account's interest total is added to its current balance (signed, 10 integer digits and 2 decimals).",
    "fields": [
     "WS-TOTAL-INT",
     "ACCT-CURR-BAL"
    ],
    "literals": []
   },
   {
    "text": "The account's current-cycle credit and current-cycle debit are both set to 0. This happens even when the interest total is zero.",
    "fields": [
     "ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT",
     "ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "0"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The updated account record overwrites the existing account record in the account file.",
    "fields": [
     "FD-ACCTFILE-REC",
     "ACCOUNT-RECORD"
    ],
    "literals": []
   },
   {
    "text": "When the read hits end of file, END-OF-FILE becomes 'Y' inside the iteration. The loop condition is tested before each pass, so the loop ends before the ELSE branch that would update the last account can run. The last account group's interest is therefore not added and that account record is not rewritten.",
    "fields": [
     "END-OF-FILE"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "Y",
     "N"
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "BR-CBACT04C-003",
  "title": "Interest rate lookup by account group, with fallback to the DEFAULT disclosure group",
  "summary": "For each category balance, the program looks up the interest rate in the disclosure group file using the account's group ID, transaction type code and transaction category code. If no record matches, it tries again with group ID 'DEFAULT' and the same type and category. Any other read failure stops the program. Interest and fees are calculated only when the rate found is not zero.",
  "given": [
   {
    "text": "The disclosure group key is built from three parts in this order: the account's group ID (10 characters), the transaction type code (2 characters) and the transaction category code (4 digits).",
    "fields": [
     "ACCT-GROUP-ID",
     "FD-DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID",
     "TRANCAT-CD",
     "FD-DIS-TRAN-CAT-CD",
     "TRANCAT-TYPE-CD",
     "FD-DIS-TRAN-TYPE-CD"
    ],
    "literals": []
   },
   {
    "text": "The interest rate on the disclosure group record is a signed number with 4 integer digits and 2 decimal places.",
    "fields": [
     "DIS-INT-RATE"
    ],
    "literals": []
   }
  ],
  "when": [
   {
    "text": "The program reads the disclosure group file by that key into the disclosure group record.",
    "fields": [
     "DISCGRP-FILE",
     "DIS-GROUP-RECORD"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "DISCLOSURE GROUP RECORD MISSING",
     "TRY WITH DEFAULT GROUP CODE"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "then": [
   {
    "text": "If the read status is anything other than '00' (found) or '23' (not found), the program displays 'ERROR READING DISCLOSURE GROUP FILE' and abends.",
    "fields": [
     "DISCGRP-STATUS",
     "APPL-RESULT",
     "APPL-AOK"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "00",
     "23",
     "ERROR READING DISCLOSURE GROUP FILE"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "If the record is not found (status '23'), the program replaces the group ID in the key with 'DEFAULT', padded with spaces to 10 characters. The type and category codes stay the same, and the program reads the default record.",
    "fields": [
     "DISCGRP-STATUS",
     "FD-DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID",
     "DISCGRP-FILE",
     "DIS-GROUP-RECORD"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "23",
     "DEFAULT"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "If the DEFAULT record cannot be read (status not '00'), the program displays 'ERROR READING DEFAULT DISCLOSURE GROUP' and abends.",
    "fields": [
     "DISCGRP-STATUS",
     "APPL-RESULT",
     "APPL-AOK"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "00",
     "ERROR READING DEFAULT DISCLOSURE GROUP"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Interest and fees are calculated for the category balance only when the interest rate found is not zero. When the rate is zero, the balance is skipped.",
    "fields": [
     "DIS-INT-RATE"
    ],
    "literals": []
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "BR-CBACT04C-004",
  "title": "Monthly interest on a category balance",
  "summary": "For each transaction-category balance whose interest rate is not zero, monthly interest is the balance times the annual rate divided by 1200, truncated to 2 decimals. It is added to the account's running interest total, and one interest transaction is written.",
  "given": [
   {
    "text": "Interest is computed only when the rate found for this category balance (DIS-INT-RATE) is not zero. A zero rate skips the computation, so no transaction is written for that balance.",
    "fields": [
     "DIS-INT-RATE"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "0"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The category balance is a signed amount with 9 integer digits and 2 decimals. The interest rate is a signed annual percentage with 4 integer digits and 2 decimals.",
    "fields": [
     "TRAN-CAT-BAL",
     "DIS-INT-RATE"
    ],
    "literals": []
   },
   {
    "text": "The running interest total is reset to 0 each time the account ID on the category balance record differs from the previous record's account ID.",
    "fields": [
     "WS-TOTAL-INT",
     "TRANCAT-ACCT-ID",
     "WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "0"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "when": [
   {
    "text": "Monthly interest is computed as (category balance x interest rate) / 1200.",
    "fields": [
     "WS-MONTHLY-INT",
     "TRAN-CAT-BAL",
     "DIS-INT-RATE"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "1200"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "then": [
   {
    "text": "The result is stored in a signed field with 9 integer digits and 2 decimals. ROUNDED is not used, so extra decimals are truncated toward zero.",
    "fields": [
     "WS-MONTHLY-INT"
    ],
    "literals": []
   },
   {
    "text": "The monthly interest is added to the account's running interest total, a signed field with 9 integer digits and 2 decimals.",
    "fields": [
     "WS-MONTHLY-INT",
     "WS-TOTAL-INT"
    ],
    "literals": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Next, the interest-transaction paragraph runs and writes one transaction record (FD-TRANFILE-REC, built from TRAN-RECORD) to the transaction file for this category balance.",
    "fields": [
     "FD-TRANFILE-REC",
     "TRAN-RECORD"
    ],
    "literals": []
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "BR-CBACT04C-005",
  "title": "Interest transaction record contents",
  "summary": "Each interest amount is written as a new record to the transaction file. The transaction ID is the run date parameter followed by a 6-digit sequence number. Type is 01, category is 05, source is System, and the description is 'Int. for a/c ' plus the account ID. The amount is the monthly interest, and both timestamps are set to the current time.",
  "given": [
   {
    "text": "The transaction sequence counter (an unsigned 6-digit number) goes up by 1 before each interest transaction is built.",
    "fields": [
     "WS-TRANID-SUFFIX"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "1"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "when": [
   {
    "text": "The transaction ID is the 10-character run date parameter followed by the 6-digit sequence counter (with leading zeros), 16 characters in total.",
    "fields": [
     "TRAN-ID",
     "PARM-DATE",
     "WS-TRANID-SUFFIX"
    ],
    "literals": []
   }
  ],
  "then": [
   {
    "text": "Type code is set to '01' and category code to '05'. The category code is a 4-digit numeric field, so it holds 0005. Source is set to 'System'.",
    "fields": [
     "TRAN-TYPE-CD",
     "TRAN-CAT-CD",
     "TRAN-SOURCE"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "01",
     "05",
     "System"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The description is the text 'Int. for a/c ' followed by the 11-digit account ID.",
    "fields": [
     "TRAN-DESC",
     "ACCT-ID"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "Int. for a/c "
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The amount is the computed monthly interest. Merchant ID is set to 0, and merchant name, city and zip are set to spaces.",
    "fields": [
     "TRAN-AMT",
     "WS-MONTHLY-INT",
     "TRAN-MERCHANT-ID",
     "TRAN-MERCHANT-NAME",
     "TRAN-MERCHANT-CITY",
     "TRAN-MERCHANT-ZIP"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "0"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The card number is copied from the card cross-reference record found for the account.",
    "fields": [
     "TRAN-CARD-NUM",
     "XREF-CARD-NUM"
    ],
    "literals": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Origination and processing timestamps both get the same current date and time, formatted as YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 (hundredths of a second followed by '0000').",
    "fields": [
     "COBOL-TS",
     "DB2-FORMAT-TS",
     "DB2-REST",
     "TRAN-ORIG-TS",
     "TRAN-PROC-TS"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "0000",
     "-",
     "."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The record is added as a new 350-byte record (a 16-byte ID plus 334 bytes of data) to the sequential transaction output file.",
    "fields": [
     "FD-TRANFILE-REC",
     "TRAN-RECORD"
    ],
    "literals": [
     "SEQUENTIAL"
    ]
   }
  ]
 }
]
